# Dev Notes 27 — Worker Layout Option C Prompt Runner v1

## Date

2026-06-07

## Branch

```text
worker-layout-option-c-prompt-runner-v1
```

## Purpose

This branch continues Worker Layout Option C by extracting worker prompt execution and prompt-message active-request lifecycle handling from `llama_worker/llama.mjs` into a dedicated prompt runner service while keeping `llama_worker/llama.mjs` as the stable worker entrypoint and composition root.

The extraction is intentionally narrow:

- prompt task execution;
- prompt message active-request setup;
- prompt final cleanup ownership.

## Source base

Implementation was staged from the formatted repository mirror:

```text
/mnt/data/runtime-dev-repo-modularization.zip
```

Active source truth remains GitHub branch:

```text
https://github.com/Main-Michael-Sparks/runtime-dev-repo/tree/modularization
```

The prior lifecycle-services checkpoint warned that GitHub HTML/blob/directory views may appear stale or mixed shortly after uploads. This branch should be verified after upload through direct source/raw paths, preferably cache-busted when GitHub views are inconsistent.

## Explicit non-goals preserved

This branch does not include:

- worker protocol router extraction;
- parent runtime changes;
- worker protocol redesign;
- model lifecycle changes;
- reset lifecycle changes;
- shutdown lifecycle changes;
- context/session service changes;
- configOverride surface changes;
- prompt/output semantic changes;
- cleanup or optimization outside the narrow extraction;
- child-process/native containment redesign.

