## Implementation summary

### `llama_worker/prompt/promptRunner.mjs`

Added `createPromptRunner(...)`, which returns:

```text
runPromptTask(record, msg)
handlePromptMessage(msg)
```

Preserved behavior in `runPromptTask(...)`:

- same-session prompts still wait for prior same-session request boundaries before prompt work;
- external cancellation is still synchronized before session creation;
- obsolete-before-session checks still run before `getSession(sessionId, id)`;
- `getSession(sessionId, id)` is still called with the request id;
- external cancellation is still synchronized after session creation;
- chunk factory creation still uses the current worker model;
- generation options still read from `state.activeConfig.model`;
- prompt abort signal and `stopOnAbortSignal: false` are preserved;
- `onToken(...)` still synchronizes cancellation before token handling;
- obsolete requests still suppress token emission;
- `stream: false` still suppresses `postStream(...)` while leaving final `postDone(...)` behavior intact;
- obsolete-after-prompt checks still run before posting done;
- `postDone({ id, res: result })` shape is unchanged.

Preserved behavior in `handlePromptMessage(...)`:

- active request record creation remains before prompt work;
- request records are still inserted into `state.activeRequests` before `record.promise` starts;
- `record.promise` still wraps the entire prompt task and cleanup boundary;
- `record.error` is still assigned when prompt work throws;
- prompt abort errors are still suppressed from worker `error` posting;
- final cleanup still sets `record.state = "done"`;
- final cleanup still deletes the active request from `state.activeRequests`;
- final cleanup still closes `record.cancelPort` in a guarded `try/catch`.

### `llama_worker/llama.mjs`

`llama_worker/llama.mjs` now imports and wires:

```js
import { createPromptRunner } from "./prompt/promptRunner.mjs";
```

Composition-root wiring creates:

```text
promptRunner
```

and keeps the inline router call site unchanged in behavior:

```js
if (msg.type === "prompt") {
    assertWorkerReadyForNativeCommand();
    await handlePromptMessage(msg);
}
```

Critical ownership preserved:

- `llama_worker/llama.mjs` remains the worker entrypoint and composition root;
- worker protocol router remains inline;
- reset/session/shutdown serialization remains inline and still uses `enqueueWorkerOperation(...)`;
- prompt readiness assertion remains inline before prompt handling;
- active request deletion and cancel-port close moved with `handlePromptMessage(...)` as one prompt-runner unit, not into abort helpers or lifecycle helpers;
- lifecycle helpers still only abort and wait, and do not delete active request records.

