## Review notes

Prompt-runner extraction was staged after lifecycle-services extraction. The branch intentionally keeps the router inline so message routing, init metadata error shaping, lifecycle queueing, reset/session/shutdown behavior, and prompt readiness assertion remain at the same composition-root call sites.

Copy-completeness focus points checked:

- `runPromptTask(...)` moved as a behavior-preserving unit into `promptRunner.mjs`;
- `handlePromptMessage(...)` moved as a behavior-preserving unit into `promptRunner.mjs`;
- final active-request deletion and cancel-port close stayed inside `handlePromptMessage(...)` final cleanup;
- cancellation helpers still abort/synchronize only and do not delete request records;
- `llama_worker/llama.mjs` no longer keeps inline prompt task definitions but still wires prompt handling from the composition root;
- fixture file lists include `llama_worker/prompt/promptRunner.mjs`.

## Caveats / known risks

```text
Finding:
  Prompt-runner extraction moves active-request final cleanup into a new module.
Affected surface:
  handlePromptMessage, activeRequests, request-boundary waits, same-session prompt sequencing, cancelPort lifecycle.
Why it matters:
  Early deletion from activeRequests would break reset/shutdown boundary waiting and same-session prompt sequencing.
Smallest safe correction:
  Keep record.state assignment, activeRequests.delete(id), and cancelPort.close() inside handlePromptMessage() final cleanup as one unit; do not move deletion into abort helpers or lifecycle helpers.
What still needs verification:
  Michael real-runtime prompt/cancel/reset/shutdown carry-forward gates before merge readiness.
```

```text
Finding:
  Prompt token emission and final done behavior were moved behind dependency-injected postStream/postDone helpers.
Affected surface:
  runPromptTask, onToken, stream false behavior, streaming/final result fallback behavior.
Why it matters:
  Small drift could change stream token order, suppress final done, or alter non-streaming final result behavior.
Smallest safe correction:
  Keep onToken ordering exactly: synchronize cancellation, check obsolete, return on stream false, chunk token, then postStream. Keep postDone after obsolete-after-prompt check.
What still needs verification:
  Real-runtime prompt streaming and cancellation behavior under local node-llama-cpp.
```

```text
Finding:
  GitHub HTML/blob/directory views may be stale or mixed after upload.
Affected surface:
  Repo verification step.
Why it matters:
  A stale view can falsely report missing promptRunner wiring or missing fixture propagation.
Smallest safe correction:
  Verify direct file paths and prefer cache-busted raw/source inspection for exact symbols after Michael uploads/applies the branch.
What still needs verification:
  Direct GitHub source inspection after branch upload/application.
```

